{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d89e6edb76ec8e86","name":"Bounding Mine","source":{"id":"source:reference-d89e6edb76ec8e86","title":"Bounding Mine","revision":17994,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T17:45:21Z","sha256":"02a6b580c28bbe630d8d4a2a2d5cf47360db4056ff8708f8fb88111e752e2b8f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=17994","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Bounding%20Mine&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d89e6edb76ec8e86","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 250\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 1 Kilogram\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Standard Mines are laid so that enemies trigger them and become incapacitated or killed in the resulting blast. These types of Mines have thousands of variations, but they all fall into one of three general categories: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Static Mines"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Static_Mines"},", Bounding Mines, and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Mines"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Mines"},". Bounding Mines are similar to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Static Mines"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Static_Mines"},", but when activated they jump up to 1.5 meters into the air before exploding and sending out fragments and concussion over a wider area.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mines are difficult to spot when they are well concealed. Visually detecting any type of concealed Mine requires a DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check. When detonated, a Mine makes a single attack roll, which is compared to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of every target in the Mine's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"}," radius. Targets hit take full damage, and targets missed take half damage. A target with the ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Evasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Evasion"}]}," Talent takes half damage from a successful attack and no damage if the attack misses.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 6d6 (Slashing)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Radius:"]}," 3-Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Splash"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Splash"},")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
